{title: Scarborough Fair}
{artist: Traditional}
{level: Medium}
{duration: 3.0}
{key: Am}
{time: 3/4}
{tempo: 100}
{strum: waltz-3-4}

{start_of_grid: Verse}
| Am | G | C | G |
| Am | G | C | G |
{end_of_grid}

{comment: Verse 1}
[Am]Are you going to [G]Scarborough Fair?
[C]Parsley, sage, [G]rosemary and thyme
[Am]Remember me to [G]one who lives there
[C]For she once was a [G]true love of mine

{comment: Verse 2}
[Am]Tell her to make me a [G]cambric shirt
[C]Parsley, sage, [G]rosemary and thyme
[Am]Without no seams nor [G]needlework
[C]Then she'll be a [G]true love of mine

{comment: Verse 3}
[Am]Tell her to find me an [G]acre of land
[C]Parsley, sage, [G]rosemary and thyme
[Am]Between the salt water and the [G]sea strand
[C]Then she'll be a [G]true love of mine

{comment: Verse 4}
[Am]Tell her to reap it with a [G]sickle of leather
[C]Parsley, sage, [G]rosemary and thyme
[Am]And gather it all in a [G]bunch of heather
[C]Then she'll be a [G]true love of mine
